  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I use the minimum displayed performance rank feature when my FPS drop to an unbearable number. When I use it, I only want the extremely badly optimized avatars gone. I don't care if someone has three copies of their avatar currently disabled, or 50 particle systems. They are not using them right now, so at that moment I don't want to block their avatars.\n\nMy suggestion is to let us decide if we want to block avatars based on the objects enabled by default or counting every object in the avatar (which is the default right now).\n\nIt could also be nice to display these two separatedly in the performance info, because I can't tell if someone has a material for every part of the body or if they have hidden particle systems.",
